From: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 02:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] make the Rust based kameleon-qmk-helper optional

The kameleon kded module ships a small Rust helper for QMK keyboards that is
built through Corrosion. Cross compiling Rust through Corrosion is not set up
in this build environment, so only build the helper when Corrosion is found.
The kded module and its KAuth helper are still built.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]

Signed-off-by: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
---
 CMakeLists.txt               | 8 +++++++-
 kdeds/kameleon/CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -111,7 +111,13 @@ set_package_properties(Qt6Quick3D PROPERTIES
     TYPE RUNTIME
 )
 
-find_package(Corrosion REQUIRED)
+find_package(Corrosion)
+set_package_properties(Corrosion PROPERTIES
+    DESCRIPTION "CMake integration for Rust crates"
+    PURPOSE "Required for the kameleon QMK keyboard helper"
+    TYPE OPTIONAL
+)
+
 
 add_definitions(
     -DQT_DEPRECATED_WARNINGS
diff --git a/kdeds/kameleon/CMakeLists.txt b/kdeds/kameleon/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/kdeds/kameleon/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/kdeds/kameleon/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ ecm_qt_declare_logging_category(kameleonhelper
                       EXPORT KDEPLASMAADDONS
                   )
 
-# FreeBSD is missing dependencies to CI.
-if(NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES FreeBSD)
+# FreeBSD is missing dependencies to CI. Corrosion (Rust) may be unavailable.
+if(Corrosion_FOUND AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES FreeBSD)
     add_subdirectory(qmk/kameleon-qmk-helper)
 endif()
